<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2108" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰᾱνής</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰηνής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>, poet. word, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεῖπνον αἰηνές</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Archil.
					38
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰανὴς κόρος, κέντρον,
			λιμός</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				1.83
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				4.236
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>I.</u>
				1.49
			</span></i>: also in Trag. (not <i><span class="en">
				E.
			</span></i>), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νυκτὸς αἰανῆ τέκνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					416
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νυκτὸς αἰ. κύκλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					672
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰ. νόσος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					479
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				942
			</span></i> (lyr); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰ. βάγματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					636
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰ. πάνδυρτον
			αὐδάν</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				941
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πέλοπος . . ἱππεία, ὡς ἔμολες αἰ.
					τᾷδε γᾷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					506
				</span></i>
			; of Time, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς τὸν αἰ. χρόνον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					572
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				9(1).886.2
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Corcyra</span>); <i>eternal</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					928
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰανῶς</span>
			<i>for ever</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				672
			</span></i>:— <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰανός</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λεύκη ἡμέρα</span>
			, and v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				416
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				479
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				672
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>El.</u>
				506
			</span></i>, is dub. (Prob. fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰεί</span>,
				<i>everiasting, perpetual</i>, hence in bad sense,
				<i>wearisome, persistent.</i>)</div>
